From: Philip Rogers <pdr@chromium.org>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:01:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/22] [M156] Defer IsolatedSVGDocumentHost::Shutdown() in
 ~SVGImage()

Original change's description:
> Defer IsolatedSVGDocumentHost::Shutdown() in ~SVGImage()
>
> This patch avoids synchronously running
> IsolatedSVGDocumentHost::Shutdown() from ~SVGImage() (such as during
> Oilpan sweeping of ~ImageResourceContent() or inside ClearImage()).
> Synchronous teardown detaches the inner SVG page's frame and cancels
> active loads on its ResourceFetcher, which can re-enter
> ImageResourceContent::UpdateImage() or allocate on the Oilpan heap
> mid-sweep while an inner image's SetData() is still on the stack.
>
> SVGImage::~SVGImage() now immediately detaches SVGImageChromeClient,
> clearing its raw SVGImage back-pointer and stopping its animation
> timer, and posts IsolatedSVGDocumentHost::Shutdown() to the thread's
> cleanup task runner with a synchronous fallback if posting fails.
> Additional defense-in-depth measures are to hold a local reference to
> the image across SetData in ImageResourceContent::UpdateImage(), and to
> upgrade the re-entrancy DCHECK to a CHECK.
>
> TaskEnvironment::~TaskEnvironment() is also updated to drain tasks,
> evict MemoryCache resources, and collect garbage in a loop until the
> main thread stays idle before invalidating FontCache and tearing down
> the isolate, ensuring deferred Shutdown() tasks (including nested SVG
> images) complete cleanly in unit tests.
>
